        "_id": "68c175468e92b2e520c8ca99",
        "title": "How to Set Up Advanced Warehousing in Business Central",
        "description": "Advanced Warehousing in Business Central is a powerful suite of warehouse management tools within \u003Ca href=\"https://plenum-tech.com/service/business-central\" target=\"_blank\"\u003EMicrosoft Dynamics 365 Business Central\u003C/a\u003E, designed to optimize storage, picking, movements, and inventory accuracy. \r\nSetting up Advanced Warehousing in Business Central enables businesses to streamline warehouse operations with precision and automation. Whether you’re tracking bin capacity, directing put-away, or enforcing FEFO, this structured guide walks you through 10 essential steps to implement advanced warehouse capabilities in Dynamics 365 Business Central, delivering clarity, efficiency, and accuracy to your logistics workflows.",
        "metaDescription": "Discover how to configure Advanced Warehousing in Business Central with a simple 10-step guide. Learn setup best practices in Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central.",
        "category": "Blog",
        "blogCategory": "plenum",
        "userRef": {
            "_id": "68661ad1a62859854fb1162f",
            "fullname": "Xntric",
            "email": "info@xntric.me"
        },
        "comments": [],
        "like": [],
        "imageURL": "http://res.cloudinary.com/dmvs9zlbt/image/upload/v1757508932/vnmuwpzfghn880pb6lyi.jpg",
        "bannerImageURL": "http://res.cloudinary.com/dmvs9zlbt/image/upload/v1757508934/hkyzkbziicttk8sz01kc.jpg",
        "quotes": "",
        "conclusion": "Implementing Advanced Warehousing in Business Central transforms warehouse operations, empowering organizations with structure, efficiency, and precision. Following these 10 easy steps, enriched by features like FEFO, warehouse classes, bin ranking, and directed workflows, puts you on a swift path to optimized inventory control.\r\nNeed help adapting this setup to your UAE or Dubai warehouse operations, or want templates for number series, put-away rules, or testing scenarios? Just say the word!",
        "subsections": [
            {
                "subtitle": "Why Use Advanced Warehousing in Business Central?",
                "subdescription": [],
                "lists": [
                    {
                        "listTitle": "Streamlined Warehouse Control",
                        "listDescription": "Advanced Warehousing elevates warehouse operations beyond basic inventory tracking, bringing in features like directed put-away, pick optimization, bin ranking, and movement automation.",
                        "items": []
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "Enhanced Efficiency & Accuracy",
                        "listDescription": "Steps such as FEFO (First Expired, First Out), warehouse classes, and capacity enforcement reduce errors, improve throughput, and ensure compliance.",
                        "items": []
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "subtitle": "10 Easy Steps to Set Up Advanced Warehousing in Business Central",
                "subdescription": [],
                "lists": [
                    {
                        "listTitle": "1. Enable Warehouse Management (Advanced)",
                        "listDescription": "Activate warehouse management in your Business Central setup to access advanced flows like Warehouse Receipts, Pick Worksheets, Movement, and more.",
                        "items": []
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "2. Define Warehouses, Locations & Warehouse Employees",
                        "listDescription": "Create the physical and logical structure: set up warehouse locations and assign users as warehouse employees, so they can post and manage warehouse documents.",
                        "items": []
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "3. Create Bin Types, Zones & Bins",
                        "listDescription": "Organize bins by type, PICK, PUTPICK, RECEIVE, QC, etc. and group them into zones. These structures guide storage and retrieval flows.",
                        "items": []
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "4. Configure Bin Capacity & Ranking",
                        "listDescription": "Establish capacity rules, by quantity, cubage, weight, and assign bin ranking to optimize put-away and pick sequences.",
                        "items": []
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "5. Assign Warehouse Classes to Items, Bins, Zones",
                        "listDescription": "Use warehouse classes (e.g., FROZEN, HAZARD, STANDARD) to classify and control storage, ensuring items are stored in appropriate zones.",
                        "items": []
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "6. Set FEFO (First Expired, First Out) for Lot/Serial-Tracked Items",
                        "listDescription": "Enable FEFO on locations to ensure picking prioritizes items with earlier expiration dates. Ties are resolved by lot/serial number and registration order.",
                        "items": []
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "7. Define Put-Away Templates",
                        "listDescription": "Design rules for where items should go, e.g., same UOM, bin capacity criteria. Templates help guide put-away decisions.",
                        "items": []
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "8. Configure Warehouse Document Number Series",
                        "listDescription": "Set up number series for Warehouse Receipts, Picks, Put-Aways, and Shipments to maintain structured tracking across processes.",
                        "items": []
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "9. Define Default Bins (Receipt, Shipment) & Use Put-Away Worksheets",
                        "listDescription": "Establish default bins for receiving and shipping on the Location Card. Enable and use put-away worksheets, group receipts and process put-aways in bulk.",
                        "items": []
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "10. Test End-to-End Processes: Receipts, Put-Away, Picks, Shipments",
                        "listDescription": "Run through real scenarios, create purchase orders with Warehouse Receipts, complete put-aways, then process sales orders with Picks and Shipments, to validate workflows. In Dynamics 365 Business Central, warehouse setup, specifically Advanced Warehousing in Business Central, is essential to modern inventory management. Whether you're asking \"what is Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central?\" or implementing it in the UAE or Dubai, these steps apply globally to ensure efficient warehousing. Use in-software features like directed put-away, FEFO, and bin ranking to align with your regional workflows and compliance needs.",
                        "items": []
                    }
                ]
            }
        ],
        "faqs": [
            {
                "question": "What is Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central?",
                "answer": "It's an all-in-one \u003Ca href=\"https://plenum-tech.com/service/ERP-consulting\" target=\"_blank\"\u003EERP system\u003C/a\u003E by Microsoft that unifies finance, supply chain, sales, and warehouse operations under one platform."
            },
            {
                "question": "Why choose Advanced Warehousing instead of Basic?",
                "answer": "\u003Ca href=\"https://inciflo.com/blogs/advanced-warehousing/\" target=\"_blank\"\u003EAdvanced warehousing\u003C/a\u003E splits inventory flows into dedicated documents (warehouse receipt, pick, movement, shipment), enabling better tracking, control, and optimized workflows."
            },
            {
                "question": "Can I use FEFO picking in the UAE or Dubai operations?",
                "answer": "Absolutely, FEFO is activated per location and works for lot or serial-number tracked items anywhere, including UAE or Dubai deployments."
            },
            {
                "question": "How do I handle hazardous or frozen goods?",
                "answer": "Use warehouse classes, e.g., \"HAZARD\", \"FROZEN\" and assign them to items, bins, and zones to segregate and control item handling."
            },
            {
                "question": "Do I need customization for automation?",
                "answer": "Basic processes work out of the box, but full automation (e.g., auto-generating picks on order release) requires customization or job queue setups."
            }
        ],
