        "faqs": [
            {
                "question": "What is the difference between commercial and promotional video?",
                "answer": "Commercial video often refers to videos made for paid advertising, especially on TV or large ad networks, often with budgets, production scales, and creative styles aligned with broadcast or high-end digital ads.\n\nA promotional video is a broader term including commercials but also online promos, product teasers, campaigns, etc. So, promotional videos often include or overlap with commercials."
            },
            {
                "question": "What is the difference between corporate video and brand video?",
                "answer": "A brand video is most often focused on building or reinforcing brand identity, values, voice, visual style, how your brand is perceived emotionally. It may sit somewhere between corporate video and promotional video.\nA corporate video may include brand video elements (values, identity), but tends to be broader (company overview, internal communications, etc.). Brand video could function as a corporate video component, especially when the goal is purely brand awareness."
            },
            {
                "question": "What is the meaning of corporate video?",
                "answer": "A corporate video is any video content created by a company (or organization) aimed at communicating more than just a product feature, it communicates the company as a whole: its mission, its values, culture, people, structure, capabilities, etc., directed at various stakeholders (employees, clients, investors, etc.)."
            },
            {
                "question": "How long should a business promo video be?",
                "answer": "Most promotional videos are most effective when kept short. Common lengths are 15-30 seconds for social media, 30-60 seconds for broader online ads. If it’s more detailed (product demo, event recap), sometimes up to 90-120 seconds, but longer risks losing viewer attention."
            }
        ],
