        "_id": "68ee3910ac08e08e2e57a4b9",
        "title": "What’s New in Bankfeed 25.0 for D365 Business Central",
        "description": "The release of Bankfeed 25.0 for Microsoft Dynamics 365 Business Central marks a significant step forward in bank reconciliation, offering users smarter, faster, and more flexible tools. This major update for \u003Ca href=\"https://plenum-tech.com/service/business-central\" target=\"_blank\"\u003EMicrosoft Dynamics 365 Business Central\u003C/a\u003E is packed with enhancements designed to streamline your financial operations, from payment import to journal posting. \r\nIf you rely on accurate, automated bank data, it’s time to explore the latest functionality that makes Bankfeed an even more essential part of your microsoft dynamics erp solution. The core focus of this version is to provide advanced control over processing logic and improve user efficiency within the platform.\r\n",
        "metaDescription": "Explore what's new in Bankfeed 25.0 for D365 Business Central, including split journal processing, advanced dimension mapping, and single-set user permission.",
        "category": "Blog",
        "blogCategory": "plenum",
        "userRef": {
            "_id": "68661ad1a62859854fb1162f",
            "fullname": "Xntric",
            "email": "info@xntric.me"
        },
        "comments": [],
        "like": [],
        "imageURL": "http://res.cloudinary.com/dmvs9zlbt/image/upload/v1760442637/etuchmrhjs9kczzwkb9m.jpg",
        "bannerImageURL": "http://res.cloudinary.com/dmvs9zlbt/image/upload/v1760442638/mouoj6tn3r7u215th9mb.jpg",
        "quotes": "",
        "conclusion": "",
        "subsections": [
            {
                "subtitle": "Enhanced Payment Handling and Advanced Matching Logic",
                "subdescription": [
                    "\u003Ca href=\"https://bankfeed.com/\" target=\"_blank\"\u003EBankfeed\u003C/a\u003E 25.0 for D365 Business Central introduces two powerful features to elevate the precision and speed of your bank reconciliation process."
                ],
                "lists": [
                    {
                        "listTitle": "Split Incoming and Outgoing Payments into Different Journals",
                        "listDescription": "Managing bank transactions across different accounting responsibilities just got simpler. The new General Journal split by Credit/Debit option automatically separates imported transactions based on type:",
                        "items": [
                            {
                                "title": "Incoming Payments (Credits): Directed to Cash Receipt Journals.",
                                "description": ""
                            },
                            {
                                "title": "Outgoing Payments (Debits): Directed to Payment Journals.",
                                "description": ""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "Introducing Formulas for Text to Account Mapping",
                        "listDescription": "Previously, matching complex bank text to the correct G/L account could be challenging with simple keyword rules. Bankfeed 25.0 now supports regex expressions (formulas) for Text to Account Mapping. This update allows you to:",
                        "items": [
                            {
                                "title": "Use multiple recognition rules for complex transactions.",
                                "description": ""
                            },
                            {
                                "title": "Control the order of application with Recognition Order.",
                                "description": ""
                            },
                            {
                                "title": "Accurately match similar, but distinct, bank descriptions (e.g., different types of 'Charges') to the appropriate G/L accounts, ensuring greater accuracy for financial reporting in microsoft dynamics 365.",
                                "description": ""
                            }
                        ]
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "Streamlined Dimensions and Simplified User Access",
                        "listDescription": "Beyond processing, this update focuses on making the day-to-day management of Bankfeed more accurate and user-friendly within your Microsoft Dynamics 365 environment.",
                        "items": []
                    }
                ]
            },
            {
                "subtitle": "Redesigned ‘Text to Account Mapping’ Dimension Functionality",
                "subdescription": [
                    "Dimensions are now fully aligned with Business Central best practices and standard dimension rules. This redesign gives users more flexibility through Dimension Priorities, allowing you to combine dimension values from multiple sources to ensure that all financial postings are coded with the highest level of accuracy for reporting."
                ],
                "lists": [
                    {
                        "listTitle": "Mark Journal Lines as ‘Skipped Posting’",
                        "listDescription": "For transactions that appear on the bank statement but do not require posting to the General Ledger (e.g., transfers between internal accounts), you can now mark these lines as 'Skip Posting'. This prevents accidental posting while maintaining a clean, comprehensive record by using the Move Skipped Lines action to archive them into posted statements.",
                        "items": []
                    },
                    {
                        "listTitle": "One Permission Set for Easier Access",
                        "listDescription": "To simplify the deployment and management of users, the new EOMDB SUPER permission set gives users all necessary Bankfeed permissions in one easy-to-manage set. This removes the need to juggle multiple permissions, greatly simplifying user setup and administrative overhead for your ms dynamics 365 solution.",
                        "items": []
                    }
                ]
            }
        ],
        "faqs": [
            {
                "question": "How do I enable the new General Journal split functionality?",
                "answer": "You must activate this feature in the Get Started with Bankfeed assisted setup. You will then need to update the Integration Setup (Bankfeed) page to select the new Journal Types for Cash Receipts and Payments before running Get Transactions."
            },
            {
                "question": "Why is the new dimension functionality important?",
                "answer": "The redesigned dimension mapping, leveraging Dimension Priorities and standard rules, ensures that your financial data is consistently and accurately coded for reporting. This is a critical component for businesses using advanced Microsoft Dynamics CRM and ERP functionalities that rely on segmented data."
            },
            {
                "question": "Where can I get support for implementing Bankfeed 25.0?",
                "answer": "You can reach out to Simply Dynamics, a trusted Microsoft Dynamics partner in UAE and internationally, for full support, implementation, and training on the new features in Bankfeed 25.0 for D365 Business Central."
            }
        ],
